  {
   "id": 16,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -1400,
    980
   ],
   "size": [
    420,
    320
   ],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## ltxv-guides.json\n\nKeyframe animation: our stills pinned at chosen frames\n\n**Does:** a guide clip (two stills + exact-black padding) + a prompt -> a clip that travels between the stills (`LTXVAddGuidesFromBatch`: batch index == frame index, strength 1.0 shared). The latent is empty (`EmptyLTXVLatentVideo`) - every pixel of direction comes from the guides and the prompt. Build the guide clip offline (see E23) - the padding must decode byte-exact black or every noisy frame becomes a guide. Host: 13B-distilled-fp8 + t5xxl_fp8 (`ltxv`), 768x768 (multiples of 32), 97 frames (8n+1).\n**Measured (E23, 2026-10-15):** PROBE - (A) same-still control, (B) full-body -> portrait.\n**Knobs:** the **guide stills** (identity lives here); **which frames** (batch position); **strength** (1.0 = hard pin, shared across guides); the **prompt** (must describe the TRAVEL, not a pose); steps 8 / euler / no STG / cfg 1 (distilled recipe).\n**Traps:** `LTXVAddGuideMulti` (per-guide strengths) does NOT submit through our sweep_workflow - its DynamicCombo sub-inputs must nest under the combo key and the sweeper flattens them (measured rejection E23). More guides = more non-black frames, no graph change. Guide stills are center-upscaled to the canvas, so mismatched aspects crop.\n**Siblings:** `ltxv-i2v.json` (S35) is prompt-only; this one pins frames.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S36** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E23** in `video/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*"
   ],
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
